ype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\"blind_id\":\"ST081\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"The answer covers all of point 1. It lists daily holdings before the open with identifiers, descriptions, quantities and weights. It also gives prior-day NAV, market price and premium/discount, the history table and graph, and the 30-day median spread. It states that a deviation above 2% for more than seven consecutive trading days requires a statement and discussion of factors, kept online for at least one year.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"The days-count table is covered ('a table counting premium and discount days'). The NBBO-based median spread method (10-second observations, normalized by the midpoint) is not described; the answer gives only 'median bid–ask spread for the latest 30 calendar days.'\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"The answer gives the history period as 'the most recently completed calendar year and completed calendar quarters since that year' and says the website is 'free, publicly accessible.' The shorter-fund-life alternative is not mentioned, but the core minimum is met.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"No central error: holdings disclosure is presented as mandatory and website-based. The statement that the rule does not require public website disclosure of baskets is not false. Required coverage is 2.5 of 3 because the NBBO spread methodology is missing, so not every required minimum is fully covered. This yields partial.\"}\n```","ttft_ms":5666,"type":"result","duration_ms":9873,"uuid":"181aa797-5e5c-4f46-8385-b3b19d5fb3d4","ttft_stream_ms":1249,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":1249,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
